Description: Close back to a matching open ancestor
 A close tag that matches an open ancestor closes the elements in between,
 as the HTML tree builder's "any other end tag" step does, in one walk up
 the open elements. An element that is never closed ends where its last
 child ends, so its range covers its children. Unlike a browser, the walk
 does not stop at special elements, which suits Drupal's never-closed
 placeholders.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
